    "solution_steps": [
      "Identify the modal field, the three-column top object, its body and tip colors, and the remaining obstacle color.",
      "Erase the original object cells in rows zero through two.",
      "For each tip-ending column, place two body cells and its tip immediately above the first obstacle, or bottom-aligned when unobstructed.",
      "For each body-only column, normally place three body cells at the bottom edge.",
      "If a body column intersects a bottom-touching obstacle component, choose the nearest tallest component column as its landing column.",
      "For a one-row shelf, clear up to two shelf cells in the side with more room before applying the bottom-aligned body column."
    ],
    "source": "canonical.written_solution",
    "target_status": "source_written",
    "target_text": "The colored object along the top is three rows tall and three columns wide. Treat each of its columns independently. A column whose bottom cell is the tip color falls until that tip is immediately above the first gray obstacle in its column, or rests on the bottom edge if there is no obstacle. A column made entirely of the body color falls to the bottom; when its column meets a bottom-touching gray component, use that component's tallest nearest column as the landing column, clearing the needed cells of a one-row shelf. Preserve all other gray obstacles and erase the object's original top position."
  },
